
# Comparison of the automatic compartment assignment with the published annotation

These scripts reproduce Figure S17 and the numbers quoted for it in Sections 2.7
and 3.6. They are a one-off analysis for the validation cohort, not part of the
Xen-Spat pipeline, and are included so the comparison can be checked.

## Inputs

All inputs are from the public Xenium breast dataset (reference 26 of the
manuscript) and are not redistributed here:

| File | Used by |
|---|---|
| `XeniumdataNiche_analysis_test_S1_TOP*.csv` (cells, coordinates, cell type labels) | `rebuild_niches.py` |
| `XeniumdataNiche_S3_TOP_*_25.csv`, `XeniumdataNiche_S4_TOP_*_25.csv` (cells with saved niche assignment) | `validation_all.py` |
| Figure 7a of the manuscript, for the annotated region outlines | `register.py` |

## Order

```
python rebuild_niches.py     # recovers the S1_TOP niche assignment (see note)
python search.py             # confirms it is stable across random starts
python register.py           # registers the annotated regions to the Xenium frame
python stats.py              # capture and purity for S1_TOP, region by region
python validation_all.py     # gap profile, capture and purity for S1/S3/S4_TOP
python figS17.py             # draws Figure S17
```

`PAPER_STYLE.py` holds the figure colors and fonts used by the manuscript
figures and is imported by `figS17.py`.

## Note on S1_TOP

The niche assignment that produced Figure 7c was not saved. The post-niche CSV
exists for S1_BOT, S2_TOP, S3_TOP and S4_TOP but not for S1_TOP, and the file
that does exist for S1_TOP has the cells, coordinates and cell type labels but
no niche column. `rebuild_niches.py` re-runs the BuildNicheAssay algorithm on
that metadata: 25 nearest neighbors including self, one-hot cell type, neighbor
sums, per-feature z-score clipped at +/- 10, k-means with k equal to the number
of cell types. It is stable across 40 random starts and reproduces the published
Table S8 coefficients to within 0.02. S3_TOP and S4_TOP use their saved niche
assignments and reproduce Table S8 exactly.

Re-running the original niche script on S1_TOP and saving the result would make
this reconstruction unnecessary.

## Registration

`register.py` rasterizes the cell centroids at 8 um per pixel and fits an affine
transform from the H&E tissue outline to that raster with `cv2.findTransformECC`
(note that the matrix it returns is template to input, so `cv2.warpAffine` needs
`WARP_INVERSE_MAP`). The two outlines overlap with a Jaccard index of 0.92.
Cells are then assigned to regions by a point-in-polygon test. This registration
affects Figure S17a and S17b only; the capture and purity numbers in S17c and
S17d use the published cell type labels and need no registration.
